  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;In the absence of a legal agreement, the proposal fails to provide the necessary financial contributions to secure adequate mitigation against the Epping Forest Special Area of Conservation. It therefore fails to comply with Policy 81 of the adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024), which aims to protect eventual harm against the SAC resulting from new residential development.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;Future occupiers would be provided with less than satisfactory levels of light and outlook from a number of habitable rooms. This is to the detriment of continued enjoyment, would harm living conditions and is contrary to the aims of Policy 57 of the adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024), which seeks to ensure that occupiers are provided with good-quality living accommodation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;Without evidence to the contrary, the proposed internal ceiling heights of each flat fail to meet the target of 2.5m. Additionally for 2 of the 3 flats no built-in storage space is proposed. This would therefore provide unsatisfactory living conditions, to the detriment of continued enjoyment of the dwellings. This is contrary to Policy 56 of the Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024) and Policy D6 of the London Plan (2021), which aim to deliver high-quality living accommodation for occupiers that meets all considerations within the required space standards.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;In the absence of a construction logistics plan, the proposal fails to take into consideration the cumulative impacts of the development on the public highway network and its users and that any disruption would be kept to a minimum during the construction stage. Therefore it is not confirmed to comply with the objectives of Policy 65 of the adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;In the absence of a legal agreement to restrict current and future occupiers in obtaining on-street parking permits, the proposal constitutes unsustainable development in that it does not promote sustainable transport and a shift towards active travel, which conflicts with the objectives of Policy 66 of the adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
